nimony's compile-time `sizeof` lays an object out as C does: it aligns a field of an object, array
or tuple type, and a field's `{.align: N.}` (#3128).

Why: a `const` or a `when` reads the size nimony computes itself (`sizeof.nim`), while the C backend
lays the object out with C's rules, so the two must agree. They did not in two ways:
- `update` rounds the running size up to a scalar field's alignment, but `combine`, which an object,
  array or tuple field goes through, only added. Such a field was placed at the end of the field
  before it, and the final round-up to the object's alignment hid the gap unless another field
  followed: `bool; (u32, u32); bool` was 12 bytes at compile time, 16 laid out.
- a field's `{.align: N.}` was not read: `u8; int32 {.align: 16.}` was 8 bytes, 32 laid out.
A binding's size check reads the compile-time size: unir-schemac's Nim bindings for unir's store
session did not compile. Hexer's `passByConstRef` reads the same sizes. Neither is fixed upstream as
of nim-lang/nimony master (2026-11-18).

What: each field is sized on its own, its alignment raised to its `{.align: N.}`, and `combine`
places it, rounding the running size up to its alignment first, unless the object is packed. A
scalar field then gets exactly what `update` gave it. A packed aggregate's `maxAlign` is 0, which
`align` cannot take, and it starts at any byte, so it rounds up to 1.

Applied to a COPY of the pinned sources at build time (`scripts/nim-toolchain.sh`), and to the
submodule for the native build and then reverted (`scripts/ci/provision-nimony.sh`); the vendored
`nimony/` submodule is never left modified. Against the submodule pin (4a965c9b). Drop it when
upstream lays objects out as C does at compile time.

diff --git a/src/nimony/sizeof.nim b/src/nimony/sizeof.nim
index 5b80b60..f138b16 100644
--- a/src/nimony/sizeof.nim
+++ b/src/nimony/sizeof.nim
@@ -28,6 +28,9 @@ proc update(c: var SizeofValue; size, align: int) =
 proc combine(c: var SizeofValue; inner: SizeofValue) =
   if c.maxAlign != 0:
     c.maxAlign = max(c.maxAlign, inner.maxAlign)
+    # An aggregate starts at its alignment, as a scalar does in `update`; a packed one (`maxAlign`
+    # 0) at any byte.
+    c.size = align(c.size, max(inner.maxAlign, 1))
   c.size = c.size + inner.size
   c.overflow = c.overflow or inner.overflow
 
@@ -76,6 +79,20 @@ proc parseTypePragmas(n: Cursor): TypePragmas =
   elif not n.isDotToken:
     error "illformed AST inside type section: ", n
 
+proc fieldAlign(pragmas: Cursor): int =
+  ## A field's `{.align: N.}`: 0 when it has none.
+  result = 0
+  var n = pragmas
+  if n.substructureKind == PragmasU:
+    n.into PragmasU:
+      while n.hasMore:
+        if n.pragmaKind == AlignP:
+          n.into:
+            if n.kind == IntLit: result = int(n.intVal)
+            while n.hasMore: skip n
+        else:
+          skip n
+
 proc `<`(x: xint; b: int64): bool = x < createXint(b)
 
 proc getSize(c: var SizeofValue; cache: var Table[SymId, SizeofValue]; n: Cursor; ptrSize: int)
@@ -124,12 +141,14 @@ proc getSizeObject(c: var SizeofValue; cache: var Table[SymId, SizeofValue]; ite
       combine(c, cCase)
     else:
       let field = takeLocal(n, SkipFinalParRi)
+      var f = createSizeofValue(c.strict)
+      getSize f, cache, field.typ, ptrSize
+      # A field's `{.align: N.}` raises its alignment to N, as C's `alignas` does.
+      f.maxAlign = max(f.maxAlign, fieldAlign(field.pragmas))
       if UnionP in pragmas.pragmas:
-        var c2 = createSizeofValue(c.strict)
-        getSize c2, cache, field.typ, ptrSize
-        combineCaseObject(c, c2)
+        combineCaseObject(c, f)
       else:
-        getSize c, cache, field.typ, ptrSize
+        combine c, f
 
